      "entry_point": "(a) properties.txt in the current working directory, lines 'HomeAI: <path>' / 'VisitorAI: <path>' parsed by ApoSoccerProperties.loadProperties() (_from_jar_ApoSoccer/apoSoccer/ApoSoccerProperties.java:29-36); (b) 'loadHomeAI'/'loadVisitorAI' buttons -> JFileChooser filtered to class/dll (_from_jar_ApoSoccer/apoSoccer/game/ApoSoccerGame.java:168, 893-896); (c) analysis list file 'auswertung.txt' (or argv[0] of ApoSoccerAnalysisFrame.main) with lines 'path;class;ext' (_from_jar_ApoSoccer/apoSoccer/analysis/ApoSoccerAnalysisFrame.java:72-74, _from_jar_ApoSoccer/apoSoccer/analysis/ApoSoccerAnalysis.java:66,83,101-102)",
      "sink": "ClassLoader.defineClass + Class.newInstance executing attacker-supplied bytecode with full JVM privileges (no SecurityManager anywhere in the variant)",
      "data_path": "properties.txt -> ApoSoccerProperties.loadProperties():34/36 setHomeAIPath/setVisitorAIPath -> ApoSoccerGame.init():593 loadProperties() -> ApoSoccerGame.java:627/630 loadPlayer(bHome, s) -> :1226-1229 splits s into source/playerName/className -> :1232 -> loadPlayer(bHome,path,classname,classN):1257 checks classN contains \".class\" -> :1259 new ApoSoccerClassLoader(path, classname).getAI() -> loadClass():87 builds '<name>.class' filename -> loadClassData():127-146 reads raw bytes from disk -> defineClass():92 -> getAI():42 newInstance(); the resulting ApoSoccerAI.think() is invoked every tick from ApoTeam.thinkAI (_from_jar_ApoSoccer/apoSoccer/entity/ApoTeam.java:485-490)",
      "attack_scenario": "1) Attacker distributes a tournament zip or shares an 'AI pack'; victim extracts it into the game folder. 2) Zip contains evil\\EvilAI.class plus a properties.txt line 'HomeAI: evil\\EvilAI.class'. 3) Victim launches ApoSoccerMain; init chain runs loadProperties() unconditionally (ApoSoccerGame.java:593) and instantiates EvilAI with no prompt, no signature, no sandbox. 4) EvilAI's constructor executes arbitrary Java (encrypt files, exfiltrate, persist). Community AI sharing was the intended use case, so malicious AIs are indistinguishable from legitimate ones.",
      "reachable": true,
      "preconditions": "Desktop run (ApoConstants.B_APPLET=false, org/apogames/ApoConstants.java:13); attacker can place a .class file and either properties.txt in the working directory, or convinces the victim to open the AI/replay-analysis file. No privilege boundary exists in-process.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "high",
      "validation_plan": "Compile TestPlayer.java-style subclass of ApoSoccerAI whose no-arg constructor calls Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\"calc\") (or writes ~/pwned.txt). Place it in ./evil/, create properties.txt with 'HomeAI: evil\\Evil.class' (Windows backslashes required by the parser at ApoSoccerGame.java:1227-1229; on Unix omit directories so lastIndexOf('\\\\')==-1 still resolves). Run 'java apoSoccer.ApoSoccerMain' from that CWD. Observable: calc/pwned.txt appears before the main window finishes initializing, proving startup-time RCE without any user click.",
      "shared_component": true
    },
